acceptance_criteria: "restore treats an unparseable existing item file exactly like an absent one and replays the requested version from history while reporting why the on-disk document was ignored; pm get on an unparseable item file refuses with a typed error that names pm restore as the remediation; A history salvage mode truncates an invalid stream tail to the last hash-verified entry, records an explicit audit entry, and refuses when any valid entry would be dropped; Fixtures cover a zero-byte item file and a NUL-padded stream tail on Linux and Windows and the point-in-time reconstruction gate replays the recovered item byte-identically"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: high
environment: "pm-cli 2026.9.4 and 2026.8.31, Linux ext4 after a disk-full truncation, sandbox tracker"
repro_steps: "Create an item, update it twice, verify the chain, truncate the .toon to zero bytes, run pm get and pm restore <id> <last-version>, then append NUL bytes to the history stream and retry"
resolution: Recover unreadable UTF-8 item documents from verified history and salvage only an invalid trailing suffix with byte-preserving audit receipts and concurrency guards.
expected_result: "Zero-byte and malformed text items restore exactly; verified prefixes remain unchanged; interior corruption, complete discarded records, invalid UTF-8 and competing writes refuse without mutation."
actual_result: "The recovery and negative-control integration fixtures passed; temporary-tracker acceptance confirmed byte-identical restoration, unchanged dry-run bytes, retained-prefix bytes and suffix digest. Windows execution remains a required hosted check before merge."
affected_version: 2026.8.31
component: "sdk/lifecycle/restore, core/item/item-format, history-repair"
